// src/hq-library.mjs
var hqLibrary = [{ "title": "Ready-to-use community copy", "body": "# Yolo Solano Veterans — ready-to-use community copy\n\nPrepared September 2, 2026 from the published directory and its recorded sources. These are reusable website, newsletter and social items. They have not been distributed, and no organization is described as a confirmed partner. Check the organizer’s latest page before distributing time-sensitive event copy.\n\n## Directory introduction\n\nFind your local veteran community. Yolo Solano Veterans brings together organization profiles and community events across Yolo and Solano counties. Explore VFW and American Legion posts, DAV chapters, Marine Corps League groups, county veterans offices and other local resources. Search by organization, location or keyword, then follow the public contact information to take the next step.\n\nExplore the directory: https://yolo-county-veterans.smartzgraphics.workers.dev/\n\nThe directory is growing. Information is checked against public sources, with missing or unconfirmed details identified on each profile. A listing does not mean an organization has joined the project.\n\n## Organization update invitation\n\nHelp veterans find accurate information about your organization. Share a meeting-time correction, public contact update, new event or organization listing through the Yolo Solano Veterans submission desk. Include the public details and an official page or public flyer link when available.\n\nSubmit an update: https://yolo-county-veterans.smartzgraphics.workers.dev/for-organizations\n\nYour name and reply email stay in the private review queue. We check submitted information before publication. Please share public organization information only; leave out private membership lists, medical information and individual veteran case details.\n\n## Short social post\n\nLooking for your local veteran community? Explore organization profiles and community events in Yolo and Solano counties at Yolo Solano Veterans. Know a meeting time that changed or an event we should include? Send an update through the site.\n\nhttps://yolo-county-veterans.smartzgraphics.workers.dev/\n\n## Newsletter item: community events\n\n**Find an event. Make a connection.**\n\nThe Yolo Solano Veterans calendar brings together local community events, remembrance ceremonies and opportunities to volunteer. Browse Yolo and Solano listings, open an event for organizer information, and download a calendar entry. Confirm attendance rules, accessibility and the latest schedule with the host before you go.\n\nExplore the calendar: https://yolo-county-veterans.smartzgraphics.workers.dev/events\n\nCalendar downloads are a snapshot, so check the live event page again before attending.\n\n## Event spotlight: Toys for Tots Halloween Train\n\n**Free train rides at Davis Community Park — October 31**\n\nThe Zombie Bike Parade Festival lists free trackless-train rides at Community Park, 1405 F Street, Davis, on Saturday, October 31, 2026, from 11 a.m. to 3 p.m. A Toys for Tots Yolo County table is listed nearby. Visit the organizer’s page for the latest details.\n\nEvent details: https://yolo-county-veterans.smartzgraphics.workers.dev/events/toys-yolo-halloween-train-2026\n\nOrganizer source: https://www.zombiebikeparade.com/events/halloween-train\n\nThis is a community event listing, not an appointment to apply for or receive toys. Toys for Tots participates in the event; the broader festival names NorCal Trykers as its beneficiary.\n\n## Event spotlight: remembrance in Davis\n\n**Remember and honor at Davis Cemetery — December 19**\n\nThe Davis Cemetery District Wreaths Across America page lists a remembrance ceremony on Saturday, December 19, 2026, at 10 a.m. Pacific, followed by wreath placement. The location is Davis Cemetery District, 820 Pole Line Road, Davis. People of all ages and backgrounds are welcome. Register through the official event page for volunteer updates and check it again before attending.\n\nEvent details: https://yolo-county-veterans.smartzgraphics.workers.dev/events/waa-davis-2026\n\nOrganizer source: https://www.wreathsacrossamerica.org/pages/174790/Overview\n\n## Event spotlight: remembrance and volunteering in Dixon\n\n**December volunteer opportunities at Sacramento Valley National Cemetery**\n\nRememberAVet lists holiday-bough truck unloading on Friday, December 18, 2026, with volunteers asked to arrive by 3 p.m. Teenagers and adults may help; contact the project coordinator in advance with your group size.\n\nHoliday-bough placement is listed for Saturday, December 19, beginning at 7:30 a.m. The separate Wreaths Across America remembrance ceremony at the same cemetery is listed for 9 a.m. that morning. Both take place at Sacramento Valley National Cemetery, 5810 Midway Road, Dixon. Follow each organizer’s instructions; these are distinct activities.\n\nBrowse the events: https://yolo-county-veterans.smartzgraphics.workers.dev/events?county=Solano\n\nRememberAVet source: https://www.wreathproject.org/\n\nWreaths Across America source: https://wreathsacrossamerica.org/pages/15553/overview/\n\n## Meeting notice: Dixon VFW Post 8151\n\n**Connect with Dixon VFW Post 8151**\n\nThe post’s public sources list meetings on the third Wednesday, with social time at 6:30 p.m. and the meeting at 7 p.m., at 231 N. First Street, Dixon. Contact the post to confirm the current meeting and participation rules before attending.\n\nDirectory profile: https://yolo-county-veterans.smartzgraphics.workers.dev/organizations/vfw-ca-8151\n\nOfficial post page: https://vfw8151.org/di/vfw/v2/default.asp?nid=1\n\nThe post says it does not own or operate the Olde Vets Hall; direct hall-rental questions through its official venue information.\n\n## Printable flyer guidance\n\nUse one event per flyer. Include the event name, complete date and year, Pacific time, street address, organizer, who may attend, and the official registration or event link. Use a large readable heading and high-contrast text. Include a short website address alongside any QR code so the flyer works without a phone camera.\n\nUse organizer-provided artwork only when permission is clear. Leave prices, donation claims, tax language, participation guarantees and partner logos out unless the organizer has supplied and approved them. If an end time or attendance rule is unknown, link to the organizer instead of guessing. Put the source-check date in the internal record rather than crowding the public flyer with technical notes.\n" }, { "title": "How we work", "body": "# Yolo Solano Veterans — working defaults\n\nUpdated September 2, 2026. These defaults turn the meeting’s intent and Aaron’s current instructions into daily practice. Aaron and Sterling can change them through Requests. They do not appoint either person to act for another organization, authorize a fundraising campaign, or create a new purchase.\n\n## Requests and routine decisions\n\nAaron and Sterling use their own signed-in identities. A request records its author, progress, discussion and result. Requests stay separate from the punch list. Chat handles clear edits to the website or headquarters, ordinary presentation improvements, research, corrections supported by reliable sources, and requested reusable content without asking the founders to resolve technical details.\n\nWhen a request affects money, a new account’s access, a disputed claim, another organization’s representation, private personal information or an external commitment, Chat completes the useful preparation and asks the smallest necessary question. Every question includes a recommended answer that can be accepted with “yes,” plus space for another idea. The request remains visible as needing input and says exactly what is waiting.\n\n## Publishing and corrections\n\nPublicly sourced organization facts may be corrected after checking the source. Record the source and the change. Use a current organization page or official directory when possible; identify missing information instead of filling it in by inference. A person’s submitted name or email is not proof that they may represent an organization.\n\nPublish requested presentation and wording changes promptly when they do not introduce unsupported factual claims. Retain a useful history so a mistaken change can be reversed. Changes to public contacts, officers, meeting arrangements or events keep their supporting source and review date.\n\nPublic submissions receive source and representation checks. They do not automatically grant editing access. An event needs a title, date and time, venue or online location, organizer, audience and reliable public source. If one detail is missing, ask for that detail and suggest clear wording for the rest. Event listings link to the organizer’s current instructions.\n\nSource-reviewed does not mean organization-confirmed. A directory listing is not a partnership endorsement. Do not imply that a host has approved the platform merely because its public event is listed. A broad launch campaign or automated distribution workflow remains a separate decision when one is proposed; it does not delay ordinary work on the live pilot.\n\n## Volunteers\n\nStart with public opportunities hosted by existing organizations and link people to the organizer’s signup route. This provides useful opportunities now without creating an unnecessary central volunteer roster.\n\nIf Aaron or Sterling requests a small project volunteer team, use simple roles such as event help, profile checking or flyer preparation. Ask only for the volunteer’s name, preferred contact method, availability and the role they want. Explain who can see those details and obtain their agreement before adding them. Keep their information in the private headquarters. Do not infer participation from a transcript mention, directory listing or attendance at an event.\n\nUse the headquarters request route for corrections or removal. When a volunteer asks to leave, stop using their contact information and remove it from the active coordination record, retaining only a minimal record of the administrative change when needed. Chat should propose an appropriate removal from backups as part of that specific request rather than promise that every historical copy instantly disappears. Private membership lists and veteran case information do not belong in this system.\n\n## Fundraising\n\nThe present platform can research opportunities, keep ideas in Coordination, prepare copy and point to an organizer’s verified existing page. It does not collect donations or make commitments on behalf of the directory or another organization.\n\nWhen the founders request an actual campaign, Chat will bring them one concise proposal identifying the beneficiary, accountable organization, intended use of funds, requested budget if any, official donation destination and exact outreach scope. The suggested starting point is to support an existing organizer’s published campaign and use that organizer’s payment route. Approval must name the campaign and permitted actions. Do not infer tax treatment, promise sponsorship benefits or invent fundraising totals.\n\n## Communications\n\nThe companion community-copy document contains directory, event, newsletter and social material ready for review and reuse. Prepared copy is not a sent message or a confirmed placement. Ordinary relationship and partner emails belong in Yahoo drafts for Aaron’s review and sending. Automatic social posting, newsletter distribution and a defined outreach campaign require their own explicit authorization before sending begins.\n\n## Ownership, costs and access\n\nKeep the current website, headquarters and source repository in Aaron’s existing accounts. Aaron and Sterling already have individual headquarters sign-in; a shared password is unnecessary. No new account transfer is needed to use the system now. Plan a transfer only when the founders ask for one, with a tested copy and a clear new owner.\n\nUse existing services and free capabilities first. Do not add a subscription, paid upgrade or new financial commitment without the applicable approval. Cloudflare access activation was approved and completed; the earlier task asking whether to activate it is obsolete. Check current plan usage before changes likely to raise costs and explain a concrete cost choice if one arises.\n\n## Work that Chat owns\n\nKeep checking remaining directory gaps: current contacts for Davis VFW 6949 and Mare Island Navy Yard American Legion 550; historical Woodland, Bryte and Winters VFW leads; conflicting DAV phone numbers; officer terms; program intake and current seasonal dates. Research may continue without a founder decision. If no reliable source establishes a detail, leave it visibly unconfirmed and prepare one focused question for the relevant organization.\n\nMaintain private database exports and source history. Verify a restore in an isolated copy before changing live data. The local recovery exercise documents what was tested; it does not itself establish a daily backup schedule or prove a cloud restoration has occurred.\n\n## Decisions only when the related work is requested\n\n| Trigger | Suggested question |\n| --- | --- |\n| A new organization wants to edit its own profile | “I suggest verifying this person through the organization’s official contact, then granting access only to its profile. Yes, or a different approach?” |\n| Aaron or Sterling wants a joint fundraising campaign | “I suggest starting with the named organizer’s existing campaign and donation page, with no payments collected by our site. May I prepare that campaign for your approval?” |\n| A wider launch or recurring public distribution is requested | “I suggest a small first group of named organizations and this finished announcement. Approve this audience and channel, or tell me what to change?” |\n| A request would add a cost or outside commitment | “Here is the finished proposal, exact cost or commitment, and my recommended option. Approve it, or choose this free alternative?” |\n\nThere is no need to ask these questions in advance merely because the original punch list mentioned future work.\n" }];

